.²1 As an alternative conjunction it means ‘or’; but its position is different
 in Sanskrit, being used either with each word or assertion or only with
 the last, but it is never used at the beginning of a clause; <ab>cf.</ab> {#ca#}.
.²2 It has also the following senses:--
.³({%a%}) and, as well as, also; {#vAyurvA dahano vA#} <ls>G. M.</ls>; {#asti te#}
 {#mAtA smarasi vA tAtam#} <ls>U. 4</ls>.
.³({%b%}) like, as; {#jAtAM manye tuhinamaTitAM padminIM vAnyarUpAm#} <ls>Me. 85</ls>
 (<ab>v. l.</ab>); {#maRI vozwrasya lambete#} <ls>Sk.</ls>; {#hfzwo garjati cAtidarpitabalo#}
 {#duryoDano vA SiKI#} <ls>Mk. 5. 6</ls>; {#snAnIyavastrakriyayA patrorRaM vopayujyate#}
 <ls>M. 5. 12</ls>; <ls>Śi. 3. 63</ls>, <ls n="Śi.">4. 35</ls>, <ls n="Śi.">7. 64</ls>; <ls>Ki. 3. 13</ls>.
.³({%c%}) optionally; (in this sense mostly in grammatical rules as of
 Pāṇini); {#dozo RO vA cittavirAge#} <ls>P. VI. 4. 99</ls>, 91.
.³({%d%}) possibility; (in this sense {#vA#} is usually added to the interrogative
 pronoun and its derivatives like {#iva#} or {#nAma#}), and may be translated
 by ‘possibly’, ‘I should like to know’; {#kasya vAnyasya vacasi mayA sTAtavyam#}
 <ls>K.</ls>; {#parivartini saMsAre mftaH ko vA na jAyate#} <ls>Pt. 1. 27</ls>.
.³({%e%}) sometimes used merely as an expletive.
.³({%f%}) indeed, truly.
.³({%g%}) only.
.²3 When repeated {#vA#} has the sense of ‘either--or’, ‘whether--or’;
 {#sA vA SaMBostadIyA vA mUrtirjalamayI mama#} <ls>Ku. 2. 60</ls>; {#tadatra pariSramAnuroDAdvA#}
 {#udAttakaTAvastugOravAdvA navanAwakadarSanakutUhalAdvA BavadBiravaDAnaM#}
 {#dIyamAnaM prArTaye#} <ls>Ve. 1</ls>; {#eka eva Kago mAnI suKaM jIvati cAtakaH .#}
 {#mriyate vA pipAsAyAM yAcate vA puraMdaram ..#} <ls>Subhāṣ.</ls> ({#aTavA#} or,
 or rather, or else); see under {#aTa#}; {#na vA#} not, neither, nor; {#yadi#}
 {#vA#} or if; {#yadvA#} or, or else; {#kiM vA#} whether, possibly <ab>&c.</ab>; {#kiM#}
 {#vA Sakuntaletyasya mAturAKyA#} <ls>Ś. 7. 20/21</ls>; {#ko vA#} or {#ke vA#} followed
 by a negative means ‘everyone, all’; {#ke vA na syuH pariBavaPalA nizPalAramBayatnAH#} <ls>Me. 56</ls>.
